    "circumstancesOfRecovery": "From Deputy Coroner's narrative (03/04/1986): Decedent is a black male medium build (5'10\") black hair. \n\nTwo men were fishing and found the decedent's body hung on rocks approximately 1.5 miles upriver toward Columbia or Blossom Street Bridge. Afraid that the decedent's body would be swept away by rushing water, the decedent was pulled 1.5 miles in water to Rosewood boat ramps. \n\nHe was clothed in a reddish-brown pullover shirt short sleeve, blue work pants, black socks w/white ring around tops. No shoes, no ID or wallet, no personal articles. Black belt.",
